@startuml M6-System-Context

' System Context: M6 Search Engine in its environment
' Shows external systems: GitHub API, users, storage infrastructure
' External actors: End Users, Administrators, GitHub, KV Store (M4)
' Demonstrates overall system boundaries and interactions

!define BGCOLOR #F5F5F5
skinparam backgroundColor BGCOLOR
skinparam actorBorderColor #333
skinparam actorBackgroundColor #E8F4F8
skinparam componentBorderColor #333
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam arrowColor #333
skinparam shadowing false

title M6 Search Engine - System Context

actor "End Users" as USERS
actor "Administrators" as ADMINS
actor "Developers" as DEVS
actor "GitHub API" as GITHUB
actor "Storage\n(M4 KV Store)" as STORAGE
actor "Distributed\nCluster\n(M1-M5)" as CLUSTER

component [M6 Search Engine] as M6

'' External inputs
USERS --> M6: Search queries\n(keywords, filters)
ADMINS --> M6: Start operations\n(crawl, index, monitor)
DEVS --> M6: Review architecture\nand code

'' External outputs
M6 --> USERS: Search results\n(ranked by relevance)
M6 --> ADMINS: Progress reports\nHealth metrics
M6 --> DEVS: Logs, metrics\nfor analysis

'' Data sources
GITHUB --> M6: Repository data\n(metadata, README)
M6 --> GITHUB: API requests\n(~100 repos)

'' Storage integration
M6 --> STORAGE: Store/retrieve\nindex data
STORAGE --> M6: TF statistics\nDF statistics\nMetadata

'' Distributed infrastructure
M6 --> CLUSTER: Use M1-M5\nservices
CLUSTER --> M6: Serialization,\nCommunication,\nMapReduce

note right of USERS
  Typical queries:
  "python async"
  "javascript framework"
  Get top 10 ranked results
  <30ms latency
end note

note right of ADMINS
  Operations:
  Start crawl (GitHub API)
  Start index (text processing)
  Monitor system health
  Check node status
end note

note right of M6
  3 Phases:
  CRAWL: GitHub API → docs
  INDEX: text processing
  SEARCH: TF-IDF ranking
  
  Supports 100+ repos
  10,000+ terms
  Distributed on 4 nodes
end note

note right of STORAGE
  Stores:
  - Inverted index
  - TF statistics
  - DF statistics
  - Document metadata
  
  Accessed via M4
  (key-value store)
end note

note right of CLUSTER
  M1: Serialization (convert objects)
  M2: Communication (network)
  M4: KV Store (persistence)
  M5: MapReduce (parallel jobs)
end note

@enduml
